                <pb facs="0783" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4023: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-06T16:00:00+01:39"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>193. Imbrie informs me of his attitude concerning military forces against
                    Petrograd. Such a move would be the height of folly and do irreparable harm.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Haynes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
